<title>RUSSIA: Russia 1996 primary aluminium output 2.79 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia 1996 primary aluminium output 2.79 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian primary aluminium output in 1996 will be 2.79 million tonnes, a 1.5 percent increase on 1995's level, Igor Prokopov, director of the Konstern Alyuminiy producers' group, said on Friday.</p>
<p>He saw production in 1997 rising by 1.5 to 2.0 percent.</p>
<p>Group data put Russia's 1996 primary aluminium exports at 2.37 million tonnes, compared to 1995's 2.11 million tonnes. Prokopov declined to forecast 1997 exports.</p>
<p>--Lynnley Browning, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
